Z||000000||FIEROMJ||04-05-2001||06:24 PM||||I posted a topic about how my car('87 Fiero GT) was acting extremely messed up a couple days ago.  Well, today I take it to the shop and I find out that it spun a bearing.  Rather than rebuild the 2.8 I would like to replace the it but I don't know what with.  I was thinkin maybe 3.4L or 3800. I don't know how much a swap would cost. I don't have a whole lot of money. I need suggestions as to what I should do. Please help!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||04-05-2001||06:32 PM||||The 3.4L is a direct bolt in swap. Just move over the Fiero externals and swap the starter holes on the 3.4L block and your ready to go. The 3800 requires some items to be made and the ECM to be hooked into it.||||reg||1
